{"repositoryId":314785116,"availability":"available","full":"stzifkas/pluto-ecss","name":"pluto-ecss","description":"PLUTO DSL Lark parser in Python","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2020-11-21T10:23:25Z","updated":"2026-06-10T07:51:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://stzifkas.github.io/pluto-ecss/","topics":[],"demo":"https://stzifkas.github.io/pluto-ecss/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:48.938Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:48.938Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:48.938Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T07:15:48.938Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A PLUTO (ECSS-E-ST-70-32C) to Python transpiler and runtime. Take a spacecraft operations procedure written in PLUTO, get back a runnable Python program.","PLUTO is the procedure language standardised by ECSS for spacecraft monitoring and command. It's the DSL operators write when they need to bring up a star tracker, run a parallel safety sequence, or react to an on-board event. pluto-ecss parses that DSL with Lark and emits a readable Python module that calls into a small runtime library."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stzifkas/pluto-ecss/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c3694a95e9d74991598fb57367346db683e1428b8421eefdf33aa1f4150f5d1f","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:49.028Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:49.028Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A PLUTO (ECSS-E-ST-70-32C) to Python transpiler and runtime. Take a spacecraft operations procedure written in PLUTO, get back a runnable Python program.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stzifkas/pluto-ecss/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c3694a95e9d74991598fb57367346db683e1428b8421eefdf33aa1f4150f5d1f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stzifkas/pluto-ecss/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:49.0